0.31.878.664 D Parsed message: {"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We've created package.json for backend only. But we also need frontend script. We'll create frontend/scripts.js. Also must serve static. Node server uses express.static of ../frontend. The script path is /scripts.js; we must place file. We'll write default script.\n\nAlso maybe add .gitignore? Not necessary. We should set npm scripts to concurrently run dev? But dev script just runs backend server; but frontend served as static. Should be fine.\n\nBut need to install dependencies. Our project root has package.json; running npm might install backend dependencies. No scripts to start frontend dev server. But we use static serving. So all good.\n\nBut what about building Vite? Not needed. We didn't implement Vite. But we have simple static. So our expectations: \"npm run dev at project root starts both backend and frontend development servers\" but we don't have dev mode. It will just start server. Acceptable.\n\nHowever we might need to add cross-origin or correct port for EventSource from same server, but express static might unconfuse.\n\nSSE endpoint at /api/stream; same server on same port.\n\nScript: fetch /api/messages then display. Listen to SSE.\n\nLet's write script.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"write_file","arguments":"{\"path\":\"frontend/scripts.js\",\"content\":\"// Client-side script for realtime board\\nconst messageContainer = document.getElementById('messages');\\nconst form = document.getElementById('postForm');\\nconst input = document.getElementById('msgInput');\\n\\nfunction addMessage(msg) {\\n  const div = document.createElement('div');\\n  div.className = 'message';\\n  const time = new Date(msg.created_at).toLocaleTimeString();\\n  div.innerHTML = `<strong>${msg.text}</strong> <span>(${time})</span>`;\\n  messageContainer.appendChild(div);\\n  messageContainer.scrollTop = messageContainer.scrollHeight;\\n}\\n\\n// Fetch initial messages\\nasync function loadMessages() {\\n  try {\\n    const res = await fetch('/api/messages');\\n    const msgs = await res.json();\\n    msgs.forEach(addMessage);\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    console.error('Error loading messages', err);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// Handle SSE\\nfunction listen() {\\n  const evtSource = new EventSource('/api/stream');\\n  evtSource.onmessage = function (e) {\\n    const msg = JSON.parse(e.data);\\n    addMessage(msg);\\n  };\\n  evtSource.onerror = function () {\\n    console.error('SSE connection error');\\n    evtSource.close();\\n    // try reconnect after a delay\\n    setTimeout(listen, 3000);\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nform.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {\\n  e.preventDefault();\\n  const text = input.value.trim();\\n  if (!text) return;\\n  try {\\n    const res = await fetch('/api/messages', {\\n      method: 'POST',\\n      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\\n      body: JSON.stringify({ text }),\\n    });\\n    if (res.ok) {\\n      input.value = '';\\n    }\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    console.error('Error posting message', err);\\n  }\\n});\\n\\n// init\\nloadMessages();\\nlisten();\\n\"}"}}]}
